codex
The four-cell table matches the handler. The registered-device failure branch has live MIPS and M88K exception calls; the `#if 0` surrounds a separate MIPS exception in the out-of-RAM read path. That path also calls an uninspected warning helper before zero-filling, so these files do not establish that narrowing always gives silent zero reads and ignored writes.
codex
Width handling adds another distinction: `memory_rw.c` truncates an access that starts inside a device; it does not dispatch the remaining bytes separately. Narrowing would therefore turn an offset-0, two-byte access into a one-byte handler call. Both candidates return the same read bytes there, so a data-only row cannot prove that narrowing occurred.
